---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import OrbitalSample from '../components/OrbitalSample';
---

<BaseLayout title="Orbital Observatory | Mars Explorer" description="Compare NASA's Mars Relay Network visualization with fixed-epoch Mars and Earth orbital samples and an operational fleet demonstration.">
  <main class="observatory">
    <header class="orbit-hero">
      <div class="orbit-kicker"><span></span> Orbital observatory</div>
      <h1>Two planets, four views<br /><em>of orbital operations.</em></h1>
      <p>Explore NASA’s Mars relay visualization, compare Mars and Earth orbital paths, and open an interactive Earth fleet simulation. Each view identifies whether its spacecraft are historical, proposed, or hypothetical.</p>
      <div class="hero-legend" aria-label="Evidence categories"><span><i class="historical"></i> Historical</span><span><i class="proposed"></i> Proposed</span><span><i class="configured-dot"></i> Simulation sample</span><span><i class="active-dot"></i> Active demo</span></div>
    </header>

    <section class="observatory-grid" aria-label="Orbital observatory panels">
      <article class="orbit-panel nasa-panel">
        <header class="panel-header"><div><span class="panel-number">01</span><p class="eyebrow">NASA interactive</p><h2>Mars Relay Network</h2></div><span class="status-badge external">NASA hosted</span></header>
        <p class="panel-intro">NASA’s separate interactive experience presents the Mars relay network in its own visualization and context.</p>
        <div class="iframe-shell"><iframe src="https://eyes.nasa.gov/apps/mrn/" title="NASA Mars Relay Network visualization" loading="lazy" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>
        <footer class="panel-note"><span>Source</span><p>NASA Eyes on the Solar System. This embed is separate from the samples below.</p></footer>
      </article>

      <article class="orbit-panel sample-panel mars-panel">
        <header class="panel-header"><div><span class="panel-number">02</span><p class="eyebrow">Mars system sample</p><h2>Orbiters, relays & proposals</h2></div><span class="status-badge historical-badge">Fixed epoch</span></header>
        <p class="panel-intro">Four historical Mars orbiters as of 1 January 2025, alongside six proposed telecommunications relays and three proposed imaging spacecraft.</p>
        <div class="sample-shell"><OrbitalSample src="/data/orbits/mars-scene.json" client:visible /></div>
        <footer class="panel-note"><span>Reading</span><p>The trails follow six hours of orbital motion from the stated date. Historical and proposed spacecraft are labeled separately.</p></footer>
      </article>

      <article class="orbit-panel sample-panel earth-panel">
        <header class="panel-header"><div><span class="panel-number">03</span><p class="eyebrow">Earth system sample</p><h2>OrbitFleet around Earth</h2></div><span class="status-badge configured">Simulation</span></header>
        <p class="panel-intro">Twenty-four hypothetical spacecraft selected from OrbitFleet’s 200-object Earth simulation, shown over a two-hour playback.</p>
        <div class="sample-shell"><OrbitalSample src="/data/orbits/earth-scene.json" client:visible /></div>
        <footer class="panel-note"><span>Reading</span><p>This sample begins on 1 January 2025 and contains no active faults. It does not show real spacecraft or live telemetry.</p></footer>
      </article>

      <article class="orbit-panel operations-panel">
        <header class="panel-header"><div><span class="panel-number">04</span><p class="eyebrow">Operations</p><h2>Mission control</h2></div><span class="status-badge active">Earth active</span></header>
        <p class="panel-intro">Try the working Earth demo: introduce a fault, approve a response, and watch how spacecraft health and customer service change.</p>
        <div class="operations-list">
          <a class="operation active-operation" href="https://orbitfleet.populationmars.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="operation-index">EARTH / 01</span><strong>Open OrbitFleet</strong><p>Inject simulated faults, approve responses, and inspect service changes alongside the telemetry used to assess them.</p><span class="operation-action">Launch console <i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></span></a>
          <div class="operation disabled-operation" aria-disabled="true"><span class="operation-index">MARS / 02</span><strong>Mars mission control</strong><p>Explore and respond to Mars relay anomalies in a future mission-control experience.</p><span class="operation-action">Coming soon</span></div>
        </div>
        <footer class="panel-note"><span>Availability</span><p>The Earth demonstration is open now. Mars mission control is still in development.</p></footer>
      </article>
    </section>

    <aside class="moon-context" aria-labelledby="moon-context-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Natural orbital context</p><h2 id="moon-context-title">Phobos & Deimos</h2></div>
      <p>Mars’ two small moons occupy very different rhythms: Phobos circles Mars in about 7.7 hours, while Deimos takes about 30.3 hours. They provide natural scale markers for thinking about the planet’s near-space environment.</p>
      <dl><div><dt>Phobos</dt><dd>~9,376 km from Mars’ center</dd></div><div><dt>Deimos</dt><dd>~23,463 km from Mars’ center</dd></div></dl>
    </aside>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(body) { background: #070809; }
  .observatory { --ink:#f3efe8;--muted:#a5a19b;--line:rgba(255,255,255,.12);--mars:#df6b45;--cyan:#75c9d2; min-height:100vh;color:var(--ink);background:radial-gradient(circle at 9% 5%,rgba(166,61,36,.17),transparent 30rem),radial-gradient(circle at 90% 36%,rgba(44,105,117,.12),transparent 34rem),#070809;padding:clamp(3.5rem,6vw,5.5rem) clamp(1rem,3vw,2.5rem) 5rem; }
  .orbit-hero,.observatory-grid,.moon-context { width:min(1480px,100%);margin-inline:auto; }
  .orbit-hero { display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.25fr) minmax(18rem,.75fr);gap:1.4rem 4rem;align-items:end;padding-bottom:clamp(2rem,3.5vw,3.25rem); }
  .orbit-kicker { grid-column:1/-1;color:#c7aaa0;font:600 .7rem/1.2 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.2em; }
  .orbit-kicker span { display:inline-block;width:2.75rem;height:1px;margin:0 .8rem .25rem 0;background:var(--mars); }
  .orbit-hero h1 { margin:0;max-width:18ch;font:500 clamp(2.8rem,5vw,4.6rem)/.95 Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;letter-spacing:-.045em; }.orbit-hero h1 em { color:var(--mars);font-weight:400; }
  .orbit-hero>p { margin:0;max-width:38rem;color:#b8b3ac;font-size:clamp(1rem,1.4vw,1.2rem);line-height:1.7; }
  .hero-legend { grid-column:1/-1;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.65rem 1.5rem;padding-top:1.1rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line);color:#8f8c87;font:600 .66rem/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.11em; }
  .hero-legend span { display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem; }.hero-legend i { width:.48rem;height:.48rem;border-radius:50%; }.historical{background:#d2b27a}.proposed{border:1px solid #bb86d9}.configured-dot{background:var(--cyan)}.active-dot{background:#72d19d;box-shadow:0 0 10px rgba(114,209,157,.6)}
  .observatory-grid { display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:clamp(1rem,2vw,1.75rem); }
  .orbit-panel { min-width:0;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--line);background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgba(24,25,27,.95),rgba(12,13,14,.98));box-shadow:0 22px 70px rgba(0,0,0,.24); }
  .panel-header { min-height:8.75rem;padding:clamp(1.25rem,2vw,2rem);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;gap:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }.panel-header>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:.1rem .85rem}.panel-number{grid-row:1/span 2;color:#605e5b;font:400 .7rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}.eyebrow{margin:0;color:#8d8984;font:600 .65rem/1.2 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.16em}.panel-header h2{margin:.42rem 0 0;font:500 clamp(1.55rem,2.6vw,2.5rem)/1.05 Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;letter-spacing:-.025em}
  .status-badge { flex:0 0 auto;padding:.42rem .55rem;border:1px solid currentColor;color:#aaa29a;font:600 .58rem/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em }.status-badge.active{color:#72d19d}.status-badge.historical-badge{color:#d2b27a}.status-badge.configured{color:var(--cyan)}
  .panel-intro { min-height:5.8rem;margin:0;padding:1.15rem clamp(1.25rem,2vw,2rem);color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.65; }
  .iframe-shell,.sample-shell { margin:0 clamp(.7rem,1.2vw,1rem);overflow:hidden;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);background:#020303 }.iframe-shell iframe{display:block;width:100%;min-height:500px;height:min(58vw,620px);border:0}.sample-shell{min-height:500px}.sample-shell>:global(*){width:100%;min-height:500px}
  .panel-note { display:grid;grid-template-columns:5.4rem 1fr;gap:1rem;margin:0 clamp(1.25rem,2vw,2rem);padding:1.1rem 0 1.3rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line) }.panel-note span{color:#6f6b66;font:600 .6rem/1.5 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em}.panel-note p{margin:0;color:#8d8984;font-size:.75rem;line-height:1.5}
  .operations-panel { display:flex;flex-direction:column }.operations-list{flex:1;display:grid;gap:1rem;align-content:center;padding:1rem clamp(1.25rem,2vw,2rem) 2rem}.operation{display:grid;min-height:13rem;padding:1.35rem;border:1px solid var(--line);color:inherit;text-decoration:none;background:rgba(255,255,255,.025);transition:transform .2s ease,border-color .2s ease,background .2s ease}.active-operation:hover,.active-operation:focus-visible{transform:translateY(-2px);border-color:rgba(114,209,157,.55);background:rgba(114,209,157,.06);outline:none}.operation-index{color:#6f6b66;font:600 .6rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.13em}.operation strong{align-self:end;font:500 clamp(1.45rem,2.3vw,2.15rem) Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif}.operation p{margin:.55rem 0 1.2rem;max-width:35rem;color:#9d9993;font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.55}.operation-action{align-self:end;color:#79d7aa;font:600 .68rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em}.operation-action i{margin-left:.3rem;font-style:normal}.disabled-operation{opacity:.54;cursor:not-allowed}.disabled-operation .operation-action{color:#88837d}
  .moon-context { display:grid;grid-template-columns:.55fr 1fr .8fr;gap:2rem clamp(2rem,5vw,6rem);align-items:start;margin-top:clamp(3rem,7vw,7rem);padding:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.5rem) 0;border-block:1px solid var(--line) }.moon-context h2{margin:.5rem 0 0;font:500 clamp(2rem,3vw,3.5rem) Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif}.moon-context>p{margin:0;color:#aaa69f;line-height:1.75}.moon-context dl{margin:0}.moon-context dl div{padding:.8rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.moon-context dt{color:var(--mars);font:600 .68rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em}.moon-context dd{margin:.35rem 0 0;color:#a7a39d;font-size:.8rem}
  @media(max-width:900px){.orbit-hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1.5rem}.observatory-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.iframe-shell iframe{height:560px}.moon-context{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.moon-context dl{grid-column:1/-1}}
  @media(max-width:560px){.observatory{padding-inline:.75rem}.orbit-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.65rem,15vw,4.6rem)}.panel-header{min-height:0}.panel-header h2{font-size:1.55rem}.status-badge{display:none}.panel-intro{min-height:0}.iframe-shell iframe{min-height:500px;height:500px}.sample-shell,.sample-shell>:global(*){min-height:500px}.panel-note{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.35rem}.operation{min-height:11rem}.moon-context{grid-template-columns:1fr}.moon-context dl{grid-column:auto}}
</style>
